[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186124590 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-63775110-b76b-5425-a979-1d472435c3ac"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-63775110-b76b-5425-a979-1d472435c3ac" :question/id #uuid "63775110-b76b-5425-a979-1d472435c3ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-107114" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R$ and its subset $A=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,a,b,c\\in R\\}.$    \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A$ is closed under matrix addition\n\nII. $A$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n\nIII. $A$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n\nIV. $A$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. If ${A}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} & {b}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{1} & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and ${A}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{2} & {b}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2} & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ are two matrices from $A,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} & {b}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{1} & 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{2} & {b}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2} & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & {b}_{1}+{b}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}+{c}_{2} & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich is not a matrix from $A.$ So, $A$ is  *not* closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is false. If $A=\\begin{bmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ is an element of $A,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2A & =k\\begin{bmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2a & 2b \\\\ 2c & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is not a matrix from $A.$ So, $A$ is  *not* closed under scalar  multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $A$ is a *not* subspace because it's not closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"IV only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a4c1e3e7-b7eb-5780-ac9f-e4101be00453"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a4c1e3e7-b7eb-5780-ac9f-e4101be00453" :answer-field/id #uuid "a4c1e3e7-b7eb-5780-ac9f-e4101be00453" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a71763c5-31bc-5501-80a5-4ad95f6b3b88" :answer-field/choices ["answer-423e1384-7818-5410-95a8-d0d39c518bd3" "answer-f4920f18-c1a5-58fd-9b3e-acfe48313d6a" "answer-6c462f0d-0366-5361-9779-d3c8686baa44" "answer-0f4db8f3-59c2-52bd-bbc6-7b8fc5889531" "answer-a71763c5-31bc-5501-80a5-4ad95f6b3b88"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-423e1384-7818-5410-95a8-d0d39c518bd3" :answer/id #uuid "423e1384-7818-5410-95a8-d0d39c518bd3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f4920f18-c1a5-58fd-9b3e-acfe48313d6a" :answer/id #uuid "f4920f18-c1a5-58fd-9b3e-acfe48313d6a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6c462f0d-0366-5361-9779-d3c8686baa44" :answer/id #uuid "6c462f0d-0366-5361-9779-d3c8686baa44" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0f4db8f3-59c2-52bd-bbc6-7b8fc5889531" :answer/id #uuid "0f4db8f3-59c2-52bd-bbc6-7b8fc5889531" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a71763c5-31bc-5501-80a5-4ad95f6b3b88" :answer/id #uuid "a71763c5-31bc-5501-80a5-4ad95f6b3b88" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-be93fcdf-31d3-5e82-b4bf-9e59c7d6464d" :activity/id #uuid "be93fcdf-31d3-5e82-b4bf-9e59c7d6464d" :activity/title "Subspaces of Abstract Vector Spaces" :a